\newlabel{tab:frontier}{{6}{10}{\textbf {Takeaway: a frontier judge shown a reference marks $82.5\%$ of genuinely correct non-matching answers as failing ($\leq 3$ of 10), against $19.6\%$ for the same answers judged blind. Scale does not rescue the failure.} Mean scores on equally valid answers, 37 $k{>}1$ items, 660 calls, rubric $a$ text identical to the open judges'. The blind row is the control: with no reference shown, the two groups are indistinguishable ($7.88$ against $7.85$)}{table.caption.14}{}}
