\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Takeaway: score blind first and reveal the reference only to correct demonstrated errors (M1). Of the protocols tested, it is the only one that keeps a reference in the loop, removes the measured inflation when several answers are valid, costs nothing when the answer is unique, and behaves the same for both judges tested. The price is one extra judge call per candidate.} What to do about a reference answer, by task structure.}}{21}{table.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rule}{{13}{21}{\textbf {Takeaway: score blind first and reveal the reference only to correct demonstrated errors (M1). Of the protocols tested, it is the only one that keeps a reference in the loop, removes the measured inflation when several answers are valid, costs nothing when the answer is unique, and behaves the same for both judges tested. The price is one extra judge call per candidate.} What to do about a reference answer, by task structure}{table.caption.37}{}}
